  "cover_text": "system requires only 12 seconds to open or close. The bottlenecks are computations and data transmissions. The setup period is around 2-3 seconds. Hence the latency is only around 500 milliseconds. A connection to the local network supports this latency.\nWhile this works in general, there may be also situations where the broadcastlatency and otheratus are undesired e.g. when high amounts of processes are started.\nThe sender runs a unique session key (or a broken key) to keep secrets with the receiver. The receiver sends a broadcastsearchkey. The receiver can then verify if the key hasnt been used for any other searches besides the one requisitend.\nThe burial data movement is",
